{ Winning by indirect attack: you leave his king alone and hit what he cannot guard enough times. You have Black, a pawn down. }
5. Qe3 { A position Capablanca, world champion from 1921, used to show pieces working together. His queen steps aside instead of offering the trade on d3, a mistake. Put your rook on b4. [%cal Yb8b4][%csl Rb2] } 5... Rb4 { Your rook on b4 lines up on the b column against his pawn on b2, and your bishop's long diagonal points at his queen side too. [%cal Gb4b2,Gg7c3] } (5... Bxc3 { Your bishop takes his knight, and you win the pawn back at once, but your best piece is gone. } 6. Qxc3 Rxa4 7. Qxc4 Rxc4 8. Rd2 { Level: the queens came off, you have your pawn back, and nothing more. [%cal Gb8b4] }) (5... Qb4 { Your queen goes to b4, in your own rook's way. } 6. Rd3 c5 7. Kf1 { Level: you are still a pawn down, and your rooks have no road to his pawns. [%cal Gb8b4] }) (5... Rxb2 { Your rook grabs the pawn on b2, but his rook takes it: a rook for a pawn. } 6. Rxb2 Bxc3 7. Rb3 { About level: you gave your rook for his knight and a pawn, and his rook now hits your bishop. [%csl Rc3] }) 6. Qd3 { Now he offers the queen trade. Keep the queens: check on c5 first. [%cal Yc4c5] } 6... Qc5+ { Check, and your queen stays on the board, still aimed at his queen side. Now watch his pawn on b2. [%tail] [%cal Gc5c3,Gb4b2] } (6... Qxd3 { Your queen takes his, and the pressure goes with the queens. } 7. Rxd3 Bxc3 8. Rxc3 { Level: the queens and a pair of minor pieces came off, and you are still a pawn down. [%cal Gc4c5] }) (6... Bd4+ { The bishop checks, and his king steps into the corner. } 7. Kh1 Bxc3 8. Qxc3 Qxc3 9. bxc3 { About level: everything traded on c3, and you are still a pawn down, though his c pawns are doubled and weak. [%cal Gc4c5] }) (6... Rab8 { Your second rook joins the b column, but your queen can be traded on c4. } 7. Qxc4 Rxc4 8. a5 { Level: he traded queens on c4, and your pressure faded. [%cal Gc4c5] }) 7. Kf1 Rab8 8. Ne2 Rxb2 { Your rook takes on b2. Two rooks and your bishop were aimed at that pawn, and only his rook could guard it: your pawn is back. That is winning by indirect attack. [%cal Gb8b2,Gg7b2][%csl Gb2] } 0-1


